sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-ceratites-nodosus-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-ceratites-nodosus-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-ceratites-nodosus-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Ceratites nodosus Schnakenberg Turing wavenumber at 26 µm (Ladinian, 240 Ma) — MorphoEval overall 81.1/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 1. Periodic Schnakenberg activator-inhibitor on an 8-wavelength mantle patch. Diffusivities are solved so k_c sits at 2.56e-05 m. The saturated field selects that wavelength (ratio 1.000). Dispersion Pearson r against one Euler step is 0.990; full-curve RMSE is 0.50 because stiff modes are poorly resolved, and the unstable-band r is 0.964. Equal diffusion decays. A gamma sweep from 1.08 to 1.90 times onset lengthens lambda from 25.1 to 28.2 µm. The shell photograph is segmented (circularity 0.659, coherency 0.522). At fixed 26 µm, Goniatites (333 Ma, 18 mm) holds 703 cellular wavelengths, Ceratites (240 Ma, 32 mm) holds 1250, and Dactylioceras (181 Ma, 42 mm) holds 1641. The fossil does not resolve 26 µm pigment. Overall 81.1/100 (faithfulness 79.4, reproducibility 85.1); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0669e59d85ea16ffd68400afdedd6a2fd1cb346e; environment: python 3.12.3, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.18.1, matplotlib 3.11.2, Pillow 13.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 84, Morphological realism / specimen match 74, Parameter expressivity 80, Morphometric validation 82, Source and data traceability 88, Code-to-model traceability 80, Reproducibility package 86. Output judged: docs/media/ceratites_nodosus_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-ceratites-nodosus-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0669e59d85ea16ffd68400afdedd6a2fd1cb346e, image/png, 490995 B, 1848×1176 px, artifact_sha256 1b02be065e72e6facf0a0217d044283bee635e8911d3e6b287a4bafaeca27bae (sha256 1b02be065e72e6facf0a0217d044283bee635e8911d3e6b287a4bafaeca27bae), spec_fingerprint cef6ede1e830551276a963350aa3ce5c67a0cb0dabe081d68214d961e5f27b65. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: cef6ede1e830551276a963350aa3ce5c67a0cb0dabe081d68214d961e5f27b65; artifact_sha256: 1b02be065e72e6facf0a0217d044283bee635e8911d3e6b287a4bafaeca27bae; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/ceratites_nodosus_turing_wavelength_s0/README.md=ae965a155c4d31c3..., datasets/ceratites_nodosus_turing_wavelength_s0/ceratites_nodosus_specimen.jpg=3c37b42ed1bd3fde..., datasets/ceratites_nodosus_turing_wavelength_s0/ceratites_nodosus_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=256f3874e2f667a0..., datasets/ceratites_nodosus_turing_wavelength_s0/paper_citations.bib=c4b089031d26801a..., datasets/ceratites_nodosus_turing_wavelength_s0/scout_manifest.json=54469d3595f1c16c...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing (1952) dispersion relation and diffusion-driven instability. | Schnakenberg (1979) kinetics f = a - u + u^2 v, g = b - u^2 v. | Meinhardt and Klingler (1987) interpret molluscan shell pigment as an activator-inhibitor pattern. | Boyajian and Lutz (1992) treat ammonoid suture complexity with a fractal descriptor. Campaign D_f values are 1.18, 1.34, and 1.55.; reconstructed_in_script: a = 0.062, b = 1.140, gamma = 1.15 times onset, Du and Dv solved for lambda = 2.56e-05 m. | 96 by 96 periodic explicit Euler integration and a radial-FFT wavelength. | Shell counts N = L / lambda at the campaign shell sizes.; transfer_boundary: The 26 µm field is a mantle-epithelial scale. Mapping its chroma onto the shell photograph is a visualisation, not a to-scale pigment restoration.; does_not_claim: That this photograph, or any published SEM of Ceratites nodosus, resolved a 26 µm pigment wavelength. | That the Schnakenberg rates were measured in a Ceratites mantle. | That Boyajian and Lutz reported D_f = 1.34 for this specimen. | That the 1.088 mm sibling slot's diffusivities were reused.." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: {'id': 'R1', 'item': 'Re-measure the dispersion with a smaller timestep so the unstable-band Pearson r exceeds 0.98 and the stiff-mode RMSE drops.'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R2', 'item': 'Add a second negative control: a domain shorter than one wavelength, where the lowest mode is stable.'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R3', 'item': 'Report a 12-bin Sobel orientation cosine between the specimen and the simulated field, and a transect bootstrap CV of the selected wavelength.'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R4', 'item': 'Expose the diffusion-ratio factor on the command line and show that it moves lambda.'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R5', 'item': 'Single photograph. The fossil cannot confirm a 26 µm pigment; that limit stays open.'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R6', 'item': 'No independent second assessor.'}" ;
        pk:hasScore "0.811"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 (builder-assessor, single agent; no second assessor)" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> .
}

